import type {
  ResultData,
  ResultSubBlock,
} from "../../components/LabFolders/types";

/**
 * Genetic engineering results, transcribed from the team's own Notion
 * results page. The three sections, their order, their titles and the
 * entries inside each are the page's own: one folder tab per entry, which
 * is how the page itself is structured (Section 0's "1. Growth
 * characterisation…", "2. Kinetics…", "3. Operating-condition
 * optimisation…", and so on through Cloning and Knocking-out).
 *
 * Figures come from two places. The phosphorus charts are generated by
 * scripts/build-genetic-engineering-figures.py from the team's own
 * spreadsheets in data/genetic-engineering/, and every number quoted from
 * them is one that build recomputes from the measurements and checks
 * against the sheet before it will write a figure at all. The gels, maps
 * and plate photographs are the source's own images, downloaded from
 * Notion.
 *
 * Four things this file settles, which the source page leaves wrong or
 * ambiguous and which its own open comments flag:
 *
 *  - The summer standard curve is read at 830 nm (the Rousser
 *    molybdenum-blue method); the 600 nm in the source belongs to the
 *    later malachite-green assay, a different measurement.
 *  - The uptake rates in the Closing are fitted over the last 45 minutes
 *    of the time course, not over all of it. Over the full window the wild
 *    type fits steeper than the transformant, so the window is what gives
 *    the result its direction and is named wherever it is quoted. Still
 *    awaiting the team's confirmation that the window is justified.
 *  - pEM7 is the promoter, not the vector it arrived in; the source calls
 *    it "the small vector pEM7", which a comment on the page corrects.
 *  - Figures 5 and 21 of the source have no photograph — both were
 *    degraded material and were never imaged, as its comments say — so
 *    those entries carry the finding in prose and no figure placeholder
 *    pretending an image is coming.
 */

